By focusing too hard on
the guaranteed kill aspect,

51
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:11,017
sorcerers raised the bar on
requirements for constructing a domain,

52
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,982
making it a more advanced skill,

53
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,860
with fewer practitioners every day.

54
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:19,677
That means this domain
is founded on packs.

55
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,780
It prevents lethal use,

56
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:26,300
prohibits physical harm, and it
requires some explanation of its rules.

57
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:31,960
You get one chance to make a statement.

58
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,640
The same goes for me.

59
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:38,940
After your statement, I will get to
make my rebuttal using this evidence.

60
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:44,440
And then, Judge Mann will announce his
verdict in accordance with the six codes.

61
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:47,601
What happens if I'm found guilty?

62
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:51,757
Unfortunately, I am under no
obligation to answer that question,

63
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:53,840
but I will at least tell you this.

64
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:55,620
After all, you have rights.

65
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:58,740
If guilty, you have three options.

66
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:02,080
Silence, confession, or denial.

67
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:05,072
Your denial may include false statements.

68
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,100
You mean I can lie?

69
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,860
In a court of law?

70
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:15,220
If everyone told the truth in court,
there would be no need for trials.

71
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:19,297
Now, make your argument.

72
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,145
Judge Man is not very patient.

73
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:26,060
I did go to that pachinko parlor.

74
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,282
And I totally played some games.

75
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:29,952
I think I even won some.

76
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:33,872
I can't avoid lying if I still
want to claim my innocence.

77
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,517
So naturally, what I
need to consider is...

78
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,424
what could be in that evidence?

79
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:45,202
There is no guarantee that this will confirm
the charges alleged against you today.

80
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:46,890
One,

81
00:05:46,973 --> 00:05:49,537
if that evidence doesn't prove
I entered the pachinko parlor,

82
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,973
I just need to deny it or remain silent.

83
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,330
No!

84
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:56,917
Two, if the evidence only
proves I entered the parlor,

85
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,657
can I say it was for another reason?

86
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:00,897
I just went in to use their bathroom.

87
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:03,457
But if the evidence
turns out to be a bust,

88
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:07,957
then I might be digging my own grave by
admitting I definitely entered the parlor.

89
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:08,870
Three,

90
00:06:08,953 --> 00:06:12,597
if the evidence proves I not only entered
the parlor, but also played the games,

91
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,980
I'm basically screwed.

92
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,200
I regret it!

93
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:18,888
But what if confessing
lightens my sentence?

94
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:22,278
Wait, does this court even
offer lighter punishments?

95
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,480
I confess.

96
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:28,400
The fact is, I entered
the pachinko parlor.

97
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:31,072
But it was only because I needed to poop.

98
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:33,121
Then I had to use their bathroom.

99
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:35,280
Is that so?

100
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,169
I'm going with option two.

101
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:40,357
I don't know if this court
accepts extenuating circumstances,

102
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,675
but this excuse is the most relatable.

103
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:44,400
Let's hope.

104
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,820
Now it's my turn.

105
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:49,180
Let's take a look at the evidence.

106
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:55,960
This is security camera footage from
the antique shop near Maji, Vegas.

107
00:06:56,960 --> 00:07:01,078
The store has an ATM which captured
this image on the day in question.

108
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:08,117
Note how striking the
resemblance, both face and build,

109
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:10,318
are a perfect match to Yuji Itadori.

110
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,957
And since he just admitted
to entering the parlor,

111
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:19,417
this photo makes it clear
that his excuse about

112
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:22,794
needing the bathroom isn't
worth a roll of toilet paper.

113
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,900
One can thus reason that
despite being underage,

114
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,717
Itadori entered the parlor with
the intent to play pachinko.

115
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,960
So then you're saying that's a crime?

116
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:36,177
The parlor had clear
posted signs explicitly

117
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:38,966
prohibiting minors from
entering the premises.

118
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:41,357
You are charged with criminal trespassing.

119
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:43,700
Article 130 of the Penal Code.

120
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,977
The Businesses Affecting
Public Morals Regulation Act.

121
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:48,766
But it doesn't punish minors.

122
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:50,750
No fair.

123
00:07:50,833 --> 00:07:51,663
You set me up.

124
00:07:51,746 --> 00:07:54,257
There was no way for me
to talk my way out of it.

125
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,017
Should I have gone with Option 3?

126
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,688
What are you talking about?

127
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,540
Japan prohibits gambling.

128
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:02,860
So, parlors and ATMs are
separate legal entities.

129
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,480
Sometimes multiple
parlors even share ATMs.

130
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:09,557
You were only on trial for
entering into Maji Vegas.

131
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:14,860
All you needed to say was, I'm sorry,
but I don't recognize that parlor.

132
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:18,472
And that way, you can deny the
charge without lying to me.

133
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:21,340
Wait, we haven't heard the verdict yet.

134
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:29,970
Guilty.

135
00:08:30,053 --> 00:08:30,883
Confiscation.

136
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,147
We're back where we started?

137
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:37,317
Now I've been declared guilty.

138
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:38,988
I don't feel any different.

139
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:49,840
He's careful!

140
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,020
What a weapon!

141
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:58,557
Not only can he make it
appear and disappear at will,

142
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:00,169
