143
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,760
Wait, something's wrong.

144
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,280
You're pretty tough.

145
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:07,760
At least I still have that.

146
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,380
Because I can't control my cursed energy.

147
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:24,420
Law Apprenticeship Period 59.

148
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:29,160
Iwate Bar Association's
Hiromi Higuruma, age 36.

149
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,697
He easily cleared all obstacles,

150
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:36,757
like the entry exam to Tokyo
University's School of Law and the

151
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:40,840
old bar exam that preceded the
institution of the law school system.

152
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,080
To Higuruma,

153
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:46,077
it was all a matter of simply
inputting and outputting the necessary

154
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:50,101
knowledge that was needed for each
individual task in front of him.

155
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,997
His peers whispered in the hallways behind

156
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:55,760
his back that he was
a genius of some kind.

157
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,040
And yet,

158
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:00,257
the gem that shone brightest
from his unlimited potential

159
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:03,980
was his overwhelming talent
as a Jujutsu sorcerer.

160
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:08,925
This technique came with
his domain by default,

161
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,897
but through analyzing his domain,

162
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:14,156
he also learned the fundamentals
of how barriers work.

163
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,780
Then, working backwards from barriers,

164
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:23,377
he intuitively gathered how to manipulate
cursed energy for physical enhancement.

165
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:26,260
And within 12 days of
awakening as a sorcerer,

166
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:29,340
his powers had grown to
match those of a grade 1.

167
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,897
Before entering the colony,

168
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:34,340
Higuruma exercised many cursed spirits,

169
00:10:34,540 --> 00:10:39,305
and he struck down over 20 players who
had the misfortune of attacking him first.

170
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:19,586
You lost the ability to
control Cursed Energy?

171
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:21,988
Didn't you take it from me?

172
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:26,517
The penalty of confiscation
makes it temporarily

173
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:29,100
impossible to use one's Cursed Technique.

174
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:33,222
So I'm guessing you've never had
a cursed technique to begin with?

175
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:38,332
That must be why the penalty switched
to blocking the use of cursed energy.

176
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:40,950
Coincidentally,

177
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:45,057
confiscation is generally a supplementary
sentence never imposed on its own.

178
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:47,860
It's terrifying to think
about how good he is.

179
00:11:49,060 --> 00:11:52,520
How can he hold his own against
me without cursed energy?

180
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:57,580
He's using his natural physical
prowess, not his might as a sorcerer.

181
00:11:58,240 --> 00:12:00,817
He must have incredibly
high physical durability.

182
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:03,665
When sorcerers lose the
use of their technique,

183
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:06,918
they often struggle with
basic Cursed Energy control.

184
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:10,735
Their instincts probably dull
over the many long years,

185
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:15,357
but the complete inability to use Cursed
Energy is even more disadvantageous.

186
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:18,497
Yet he can still fight this
well under these circumstances.

187
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:22,815
My first strike would have usually
settled the battle against most foes.

188
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:25,500
If I'm not careful, I'll trip me up.

189
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,720
I'll crush him with my full might.

190
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:10,599
You're incredible.

191
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:14,218
It's like I'm fighting some
kind of unbreakable doll.

192
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:16,360
Shit, shit, shit, shit.

193
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,052
How long will this last?

194
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:19,712
I need my cursed energy.

195
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,000
Come back to me.

196
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:23,284
He's got such a strong ability.

197
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,417
There must be something I can do.

198
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:28,117
There's something that puts
Higuruma at a disadvantage!

199
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,030
Think!

200
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,560
Think? Think!

201
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,280
A technique for court trials.

202
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,030
Trials!

203
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:43,970
Higuruma!

204
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:46,300
I want a retrial!

205
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,800
You figured it out.

206
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,037
That was close.

207
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,940
I get a second trial, right?

208
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:09,097
As long as the targeted defendant
never actually admitted their guilt,

209
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:11,197
even after having previously been found

210
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:13,927
guilty and subjected to
penalty by Judge Man?

211
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:17,120
they are entitled to
demand up to two retrials.

212
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:21,340
Judge Man is incapable of
refusing such a request.

213
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,540
I demand a do-over!

214
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:30,340
The court calls Yuji Itadori.

215
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:35,660
You stand accused of mass murder in
Shibuya on the night of Halloween,

216
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:38,020
October City, 2018.

217
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:44,377
Yeah, I killed all of them.

218
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:45,931
I'm not going to deny it.

219
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:52,537
Guilty! Confestation!

220
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:54,240
Death Penalty!

221
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:00,630
Higuruma.

222
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:08,830
Yoshizawa.

223
00:15:08,913 --> 00:15:12,818
I've already submitted the proposal,
if that's what you're here about.

224
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:15,277
No, I'm not here about that.

225
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,240
I took a look at the documents.

226
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,579
They're wonderful.

227
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:22,333
Good enough as is for the
judge to use in his sentencing.

228
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:28,427
You wanted to be either a public prosecutor
or a defense lawyer, is that right?

229
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,030
Yes.

230
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,252
Consider something else.

231
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:36,121
How would you feel about
becoming a judge instead?

232
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:48,660
The heaviest sentence Judge
Man can impose on the guilty

233
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:53,520
is confiscation accompanied
by the death penalty.

234
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:59,737
Confiscation makes it impossible for
the guilty party to use their technique,

235
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:02,660
or in Itadori's case,
control his cursed energy.

236
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:07,040
As prosecutor, Higuruma is
granted the executioner's sword.

237
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:12,900
Anyone cut by the
Executioner's sword will,

238
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:16,060
without exception, meet
their untimely death.

239
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:22,140
Being empathetic to another person's
feelings means understanding their weakness.

240
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,940
The weakness of victims.

241
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:26,980
The weakness of criminals.

242
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:30,560
Day after day after day.

243
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:33,860
I was so fed up with everything.

244
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,080
So ugly.

245
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:39,117
That's what I started to think every time

246
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:41,729
I tried to help someone
who needed a break.

247
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:44,240
Just like you, Itadori!

248
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:49,140
All people are weak and ugly!

249
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:53,053
No matter how much you long
for them to have noble souls!

250
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:58,154
There's nothing for you down that path!

251
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,496
The darkness before you is just that!

252
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:06,920
Even if you shine a light on it,
you'll just find blinding nothingness!

253
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:14,797
I'm sorry.

254
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:16,840
I don't want to become a judge.

255
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:23,650
I see.

256
00:17:23,733 --> 00:17:25,800
May I ask why you feel this way?

257
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:30,140
All people are weak and ugly.

258
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:36,500
I'm not interested in promotions,
so I'm not cut out for it.

259
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:41,700
However, at the time, at
least up until that moment,

260
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:45,817
I believed that the very
depravity which no other

261
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:48,606
creatures possessed was
meant to be cherished.

262
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,230
Why?

263
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:54,760
Yuji Itadori, why did
you admit your guilt?

264
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:58,797
The evidence that Judge Man
submits is shared with the sorcerer

265
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:02,777
before it is revealed to the defendant
during the course of the trial.

266
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:08,400
The evidence Judge-Man provided was about
the demon harbored inside you, Sukuna!

267
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,280
You didn't kill them!

268
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:14,140
So why? Why?!

269
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:34,360
Uh, hey.

270
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:39,260
Penal Code Article 39, Clause 1.

271
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:43,317
Being deprived of either
sound judgment or control

272
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:47,140
of one's actions qualifies
as non-compost mentis.

273
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:53,461
That night in Shibuya, Sukuna took
control of your body, didn't he?

274
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:55,366
How do you know about Sukuna?

275
00:18:58,620 --> 00:19:03,280
In other words, you lacked
control of your actions.

276
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:06,197
You didn't voluntarily
surrender control either.

277
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,197
And so, you're innocent.

278
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:10,000
You've committed no crime.

279
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,557
Regardless of all that,
it's still my fault.

280
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:17,800
Because I was too weak to stop him.

281
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:22,900
I see.

282
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:28,278
Igaruma, why did you release
your technique just now?

283
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:33,560
I wanted to return to my roots.

284
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:41,037
Itadori, there may still be plenty of
people who are weak and ugly like you,

285
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:42,708
wandering around out there.

286
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:46,980
Put your shirt back on, then have a seat.

287
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:49,161
I'm giving you my hundred points.

288
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:08,615
Itadori, have you ever killed someone
by your own will and not a Sukuna?

289
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:16,820
I have.

290
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:25,717
I see.

291
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,540
Didn't it feel awful?

292
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:57,217
I'll

293
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:58,617
see

294
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:04,337
you

295
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:07,180
next time.

296
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:25,337
I don't know if it's not a war.

297
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:27,137
I don't know if it's all.

298
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:30,957
It's all for the end of the day.

299
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:32,757
I'm going to leave you here.

300
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:34,760
I don't want to lose you.

301
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:37,960
But I'm scared of it.

302
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:39,697
I'm going to lose you.

303
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:40,877
I'm going to lose you.

304
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:42,357
I'm going to get you.

305
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:47,237
but I'm not in the corner of my head.

306
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:48,677
I'm going to keep looking.

307
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:50,700
I'm going to take you.

308
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:02,120
Kogane, add a new rule.

309
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:06,200
Make possible the transfer
of points between players.

310
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:08,660
Of course,

311
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:12,757
this should count toward the change in
points mentioned in rule number eight.

312
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:14,380
Approved! Rule added.

313
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:15,717
Rule number ten.

314
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:18,477
Players are able to
transfer a number of points

315
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:21,325
of their choosing to
other players in the game.

316
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:25,280
Kogane, give one of my points to Itadori.

317
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,060
As you wish.

318
00:22:29,420 --> 00:22:33,100
You have been granted one
point by Hiromi Higuruma.

319
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,857
Now neither of us will have to worry about

320
00:22:35,940 --> 00:22:38,411
our techniques being stripped for 19 days.

321
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:40,120
Take care.

322
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:44,091
Higuruma, what are you planning to do now?

323
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:46,077
You could join us if you want.

324
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:48,042
We'd be stronger with your help.

325
00:22:49,420 --> 00:22:52,777
My two remaining points
are from the judge and

326
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:55,940
prosecutor that I killed
before coming to Tokyo.

327
00:22:56,780 --> 00:23:00,660
Once the barriers open up, I
think I might turn myself in.

328
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:04,260
Until then, I'll think
about what I should do next.

329
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:09,860
Besides, if I stay with you, I'm
likely to hate myself even more.

330
00:23:11,900 --> 00:23:13,724
Sorry, I'm not criticizing you.

331
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:16,500
See you later.

332
00:23:39,860 --> 00:23:40,011
Thank you.
